{"kind":"request","text":"R7 hardening follow-ups (under 6dd06d03; checker verdict 21c4328b, Security\nlimits 2 and 3, rollout notes 2a and 3).\n\nWork, one head after BR-3 and BR-9, before the certified cohort is enabled:\n1. Record size. Tie the certifiedPublicationState passes-record ceiling to\n   the entry bound (Bounds.entryBytes, 256 KiB) so a policy that the\n   decoder admits can never produce an unwritable record, or prove with a\n   witness at the largest admissible policy that the record fits. State\n   which, with the measured largest record.\n2. Certification liveness. A certificate request is left unanswered when\n   any other entry lands in the destination during the tree read. Give the\n   member a deterministic answer (a refusal naming the intervening entry)\n   instead of silence, so a retry is a decision and not a guess. A member\n   repeating entries on purpose stays a liveness limit; record it.\n3. Certificate reuse. A certificate binds one commit and is never marked\n   used, so a proposal can be published again later with it. Decide and\n   implement one of: the certificate is accepted only while the\n   destination head equals the head at certification, or it is marked used\n   by its first publication. Say why.\n4. Page wording. The rules summary says \"Use the certified rules workflow\n   to change them\" but no user-facing publish path for Rules 11 ships.\n   Name the real command when it exists or reword to what a member can do\n   today.\n\nWitnesses: a maximum-size policy fits (or is refused before capture); a\ncertificate request with an intervening entry gets its named refusal; a\nsecond publication with a used or stale certificate is refused with its\nreason; the Page text matches the shipped commands.\n\nOrdinary gate at the exact head; PD-2 note and manifest; one checker review\nbefore landing. No deployment; the planner schedules the cohort.","body":{"conditions":"One head; ordinary gate at the exact head; PD-2 note and manifest; named witnesses with paired controls; one checker review at the exact head before landing; no deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}